`mappings` (line 81) and `existing` (line 106) are read on `db`, then the add/remove run inside `db.Transaction(...)`. Two concurrent logins for the same user can interleave between the read and the write. It's effectively benign here (login reconcile is best-effort, and the insert uses `OnConflict DoNothing`), but moving the two reads inside the transaction would make the reconcile atomic. Non-blocking.
